      },
      "message": "fix(circular): judge a whole-model Circular against the finished part\n\nA Circular whose source is the finished part (SrcRef::Entity, part_solid)\ntook DepthLaw::None, so a circle typed through the part's wall generated\nwith no warning on the operation; only the program-level stock sim held\nthe post. It now takes DepthLaw::Section through one shared law,\nauthored_law(src), written for the kinds that cut geometry typed by hand\n(Circular now, the Slot of #1537 next): an Entity source is judged, a\nStock source still cuts unjudged, a picked Circular keeps its law.\n\nPinned by circular_entity_law.rs (wall convicted and the post blocked,\nlegal circle clean and path unchanged, Stock unjudged, MCP parity) and\noperation::authored_law_tests (the law table).\n\nFixes #1543\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
